bertiniParameterHomotopy -- a main method to perform a parameter homotopy in Bertini
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = bertiniParameterHomotopy(F,P,T)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of polynomials
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of parameter
        indeterminants
      * T, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of lists of target
        parameter values
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AffVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * *note B'Constants: B'Constants, => ..., default value {}, an option to
        designate the constants for a Bertini Input file
      * B'Functions (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * BertiniInputConfiguration (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        {},
      * *note HomVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * M2Precision (missing documentation) => ..., default value 53, 
      * OutputStyle (missing documentation) => ..., default value "OutPoints", 
      * *note RandomComplex: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers,
        => ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * *note RandomReal: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers, =>
        ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * *note TopDirectory: TopDirectory, => ..., default value
        "/tmp/M2-44572-0/0", Option to change directory for file storage.
      * *note Verbose: bertiniTrackHomotopy_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, Option to silence additional output
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list whose entries are lists of
        solutions for each target system

Description
===========

This method numerically solves several polynomial systems from a parameterized
family at once.  The list F is a system of polynomials in ring variables and
the parameters listed in P.  The list T is the set of parameter values for
which solutions to F are desired.  Both stages of Bertini's parameter homotopy
method are called with bertiniParameterHomotopy. First, Bertini assigns a
random complex number to each parameter and solves the resulting system, then,
after this initial phase, Bertini computes solutions for every given choice of
parameters using a number of paths equal to the exact root count in the first
