bertiniSample -- a main method to sample points from an irreducible component of a variety
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        V = bertiniSample (n, W)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer specifying the
        number of desired sample points
      * W, a *note witness set: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet,, a witness set for an
        irreducible component
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BertiniInputConfiguration (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        {},
      * *note IsProjective: IsProjective, => ..., default value -1, optional
        argument to specify whether to use homogeneous coordinates
      * *note Verbose: bertiniTrackHomotopy_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, Option to silence additional output
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of sample points

Description
===========

Samples points from an irreducible component of a variety using Bertini.  The
irreducible component needs to be in its numerical form as a *note WitnessSet:
(NAGtypes)WitnessSet,.  The method *note bertiniPosDimSolve:
bertiniPosDimSolve, can be used to generate a witness set for the component.
Bertini (1) writes the witness set to a temporary file, (2) invokes Bertini's
solver with option TrackType => 2, and (3 moves the hyperplanes defined in the
*note WitnessSet: (NAGtypes)WitnessSet, W within the space until the desired
points are sampled, (4) stores the output of Bertini in a temporary file, and
finally (5) parses and outputs the solutions.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = { (y^2+x^2+z^2-1)*x, (y^2+x^2+z^2-1)*y }                            |
|                                                                             |
|       3      2      2       2     3      2                                  |
|o2 = {x  + x*y  + x*z  - x, x y + y  + y*z  - y}                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : NV = bertiniPosDimSolve(F)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = NV                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NumericalVariety                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
