bertiniZeroDimSolve -- a main method to solve a zero-dimensional system of equations
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = bertiniZeroDimSolve F
        S = bertiniZeroDimSolve I
        S = bertiniZeroDimSolve(I, UseRegeneration=>1)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of ring elements (system
        need not be square)
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal defining a variety
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AffVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * *note B'Constants: B'Constants, => ..., default value {}, an option to
        designate the constants for a Bertini Input file
      * B'Functions (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * BertiniInputConfiguration (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        {},
      * *note HomVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * IsProjective (missing documentation) => ..., default value -1, 
      * M2Precision (missing documentation) => ..., default value 53, 
      * NameMainDataFile (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        "main_data",
      * NameSolutionsFile (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        "raw_solutions",
      * OutputStyle (missing documentation) => ..., default value "OutPoints", 
      * *note RandomComplex: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers,
        => ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * *note RandomReal: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers, =>
        ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * *note TopDirectory: TopDirectory, => ..., default value
        "/tmp/M2-44572-0/0", Option to change directory for file storage.
      * UseRegeneration (missing documentation) => ..., default value -1, 
      * *note Verbose: bertiniTrackHomotopy_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, Option to silence additional output
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of points that are
        contained in the variety of F

Description
===========

This method finds isolated solutions to the system F via numerical polynomial
homotopy continuation by (1) building a Bertini input file from the system F,
(2) calling Bertini on this input file, (3) returning solutions from a machine
readable file that is an output from Bertini.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2-1,y^2-2};                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = bertiniZeroDimSolve F                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = {{1, 1.41421}, {1, -1.41421}, {-1, 1.41421}, {-1, -1.41421}}|
|                                                                 |
|o3 : List                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

Each solution is of type *note Point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,.  Additional
information about the solution can be accessed by using *note peek:
(Macaulay2Doc)peek,.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : peek S_0                            |
|                                         |
|o4 = Point{cache => CacheTable{...14...}}|
|           Coordinates => {1, 1.41421}   |
+-----------------------------------------+

Bertini uses a multihomogeneous homotopy as a default, but regeneration can be
deployed with the option UseRegeneration=>1 .

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = CC[x];                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : F = {x^2*(x-1)};                             |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = bertiniZeroDimSolve F                    |
|                                                  |
|o7 = {{1}, {-1.55589e-15-2.46051e-15*ii}}         |
|                                                  |
|o7 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : B = bertiniZeroDimSolve(F,UseRegeneration=>1)|
|                                                  |
|o8 = {{1}}                                        |
|                                                  |
|o8 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Variables must begin with a letter (lowercase or capital) and can only contain
letters, numbers, underscores, and square brackets. Regeneration in
bertiniZeroDimSolve only finds nonsingular isolated points.

