makeB'InputFile -- write a Bertini input file in a directory
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        makeB'InputFile(s)
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, a directory where the input
        file will be written
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AffVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * *note B'Constants: B'Constants, => ..., default value {}, an option to
        designate the constants for a Bertini Input file
      * B'Functions (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * B'Polynomials (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * BertiniInputConfiguration (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        {},
      * *note HomVariableGroup: Variable groups, => ..., default value {}, an
        option to group variables and use multihomogeneous homotopies
      * NameB'InputFile (missing documentation) => ..., default value "input", 
      * NamePolynomials (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * ParameterGroup (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * PathVariable (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * *note RandomComplex: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers,
        => ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * *note RandomReal: Bertini input file declarations_co random numbers, =>
        ..., default value {}, an option which designates
        symbols/strings/variables that will be set to be a random real number
        or random complex number
      * SetParameterGroup (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * StorageFolder (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * VariableList (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * *note Verbose: bertiniTrackHomotopy_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, Option to silence additional output

Description
===========

This function writes a Bertini input file. The user can specify CONFIGS for the
file using the BertiniInputConfiguration option. The user should specify
variable groups with the AffVariableGroup (affine variable group) option or
HomVariableGroup (homogeneous variable group) option. The user should specify
the polynomial system they want to solve with the  B'Polynomials option or
B'Functions option. If B'Polynomials is not used then the user should use the
NamePolynomials option.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x1,x2,y]                                         |
|                                                           |
|o1 = R                                                     |
|                                                           |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : theDir = temporaryFileName();                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : makeDirectory theDir                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : makeB'InputFile(theDir,                               |
|             BertiniInputConfiguration=>{MPType=>2},       |
|         AffVariableGroup=>{{x1,x2},{y}},                  |
|             B'Polynomials=>{y*(x1+x2+1)^2+1,x1-x2+1,y-2});|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R=QQ[x1,x2,y,X]                                |
|                                                    |
|o5 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : makeB'InputFile(theDir,                        |
|             BertiniInputConfiguration=>{MPType=>2},|
|         AffVariableGroup=>{{x1,x2},{y}},           |
|             NamePolynomials=>{f1,f2,f3},           |
|             B'Functions=>{                         |
|            {X,x1+x2+1},                            |
|            {f1,y*X^2+1},                           |
|            {f2,x1-x2+1},                           |
|            {f3,y-2}});                             |
+----------------------------------------------------+
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R=QQ[x1,x2,y,X]                                |
|                                                    |
|o7 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : makeB'InputFile(theDir,                        |
|              BertiniInputConfiguration=>{MPype=>2},|
|          AffVariableGroup=>{{x1,x2},{y}},          |
|               B'Polynomials=>{y*X^2+1,x1-x2+1,y-2},|
|                B'Functions=>{                      |
|                   {X,x1+x2+1}});                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+

Variables must begin with a letter (lowercase or capital) and can only contain
letters, numbers, underscores, and square brackets. "jade" should not be used
in any expression. "I" can only be used to represent the complex number
sqrt(-1).

